nue  working with you and thank you for  agreeing to do this i'm definitely  humbled  i thank you for allowing me the  opportunity to even open up  and show that other side yeah chief  green's working really hard you know  pine lake they say it's predominantly  white but the surrounding area is 90  black right and so the the complaint was  90  of the complaints were about police  profiling the black community  who were not residents but they were  getting the majority of the tickets yeah  the overwhelming majority of tickets  were going to  people of color yeah and zachary's  saying to that young man we're gonna get  your tire fixed  that's a really key thing because when  you have predatory ticketing  every little thing on your car becomes a  fine if you don't pay the plane it rolls  into something else you can lose your  license  big problems result yep major issue  filmmaker says the council is blind to  institutional racism and excuses it away  they're not tackling it  clearly they want to do something about  that you can watch the cbsn originals  documentary welcome to pine lake this  sunday night at 8 7 central  on cbs
 

